        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 72-year-old male, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he showed significant dyspnoea, reduced oxygen saturation, and increased sputum production. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without evidence of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia with compensated respiratory acidosis. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement of respiratory function. He was discharged in stable condition with instructions to continue inhaled bronchodilators and a short course of oral steroids. We recommend close follow-up and optimisation of his COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
